{"id":"s6","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":13,"of":14,"title":"Written and spoken","titleHe":"מִשְׁלָב","goal":"Read the formal forms that speech has dropped.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Written Hebrew keeps forms that conversation has abandoned. Neither is more correct — but a book uses the left column, and you will not have heard it."},{"type":"table","caption":"Same meaning, two registers","head":["written","spoken","meaning"],"rows":[["אֲשֶׁר","שֶׁ","that, which"],["אֵינֶנִּי יוֹדֵעַ","אֲנִי לֹא יוֹדֵעַ","I don't know"],["בֵּיתִי","הַבַּיִת שֶׁלִּי","my house"],["כַּאֲשֶׁר","כְּשֶׁ","when"],["רַבִּים","הַרְבֵּה","many"],["הִנֵּה","הִנֵּה / זֶה","here is"]]},{"type":"text","body":"The possessive suffix is the one to know: instead of הַבַּיִת שֶׁלִּי, literary Hebrew attaches the pronoun to the noun."},{"type":"table","caption":"Possessive suffixes","head":["form","meaning"],"rows":[["בֵּיתִי","my house"],["בֵּיתְךָ","your (m.) house"],["בֵּיתוֹ","his house"],["בֵּיתָהּ","her house"],["שְׁמוֹ","his name"],["יָדָהּ","her hand"],["דְּבָרַי","my words"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֵינֶנִּי","en":"I am not (literary)","translit":"eineni"},{"he":"כַּאֲשֶׁר","en":"when (literary)","translit":"ka'asher"},{"he":"הִנֵּה","en":"here is, behold","translit":"hine"},{"he":"בֵּיתוֹ","en":"his house","translit":"beito"},{"he":"שְׁמוֹ","en":"his name","translit":"shmo"},{"he":"דָּבָר","en":"thing, word","translit":"davar"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["children","goes down","I am not (literary)","hour, o'clock"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אֵינֶנִּי","translit":"eineni"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["face","when (literary)","lacking, defective","man"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כַּאֲשֶׁר","translit":"ka'asher"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["the moment that","learns, studies","stomach, belly","here is, behold"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הִנֵּה","translit":"hine"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["his house","hates","pink","even"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֵּיתוֹ","translit":"beito"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["conclusion","his name","wait! (m.)","green (f.)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שְׁמוֹ","translit":"shmo"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["people, men","thing, word","twelve (m.)","world"],"correct":1,"prompt":"דָּבָר","translit":"davar"},{"type":"choice","q":"Possessive suffixes — דְּבָרַי?","options":["his house","my house","my words","your (m.) house"],"correct":2,"he":false},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["כַּאֲשֶׁר","דָּבָר","אֵינֶנִּי","הִנֵּה"],"correct":0,"say":"כַּאֲשֶׁר","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אֵינֶנִּי","I am not (literary)"],["כַּאֲשֶׁר","when (literary)"],["הִנֵּה","here is, behold"],["בֵּיתוֹ","his house"],["שְׁמוֹ","his name"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “thing, word”?","options":["אוֹכֵל","שׁוֹפָר","דָּבָר","עֵט"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Same meaning, two registers — רַבִּים?","options":["I don't know","many","my house","that, which"],"correct":1,"he":false},{"type":"choice","q":"Same meaning, two registers — אֵינֶנִּי יוֹדֵעַ?","options":["that, which","when","my house","I don't know"],"correct":3,"he":false},{"type":"choice","q":"Possessive suffixes — בֵּיתְךָ?","options":["my house","her house","his house","your (m.) house"],"correct":3,"he":false},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “when (literary)”?","options":["כַּאֲשֶׁר","מִצַּד אֶחָד","מֶמְשָׁלָה","רוֹאֶה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"דָּבָר","translit":"davar","en":"thing, word"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “his house” in Hebrew","answer":"בֵּיתוֹ","hint":"beito"}]}